#
# Scheduled tasks that assert-ci-toolchain.ps1 -ExpectBackgroundServicesOff
# STARTS on the clone before it checks the ci-background-off services, so a
# task that re-enables Windows Update is caught by the gate instead of ~6 min
# into a job (which is how the first version of this payload slipped through).
# One task path per line. Measured on 2026-09-30 on a clone of the golden,
# each started by hand and wuauserv read back 75 s later:
#   InstallService\ScanForUpdates   re-enabled + started wuauserv (the culprit;
#                                     fixed by disabling InstallService)
#   InstallService\SmartRetry, ScanForUpdatesAsUser   no change
#   UpdateOrchestrator\Schedule Scan, Start Oobe Expedite Work,
#   WaaSMedic\PerformRemediation      0x80070422 (their service is disabled)
#   UpdateOrchestrator\USO_UxBroker   0x80070002, no change
#   WindowsUpdate\Scheduled Start     refuses an on-demand start (it only runs
#                                     `sc start wuauserv`, which fails while
#                                     wuauserv is Disabled)
\Microsoft\Windows\InstallService\ScanForUpdates
\Microsoft\Windows\InstallService\ScanForUpdatesAsUser
\Microsoft\Windows\InstallService\SmartRetry
\Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\Schedule Scan
\Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\Start Oobe Expedite Work
\Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\USO_UxBroker
\Microsoft\Windows\WaaSMedic\PerformRemediation
